// Addon packs and addon settings UI.

%locale: 
%namespace: addon

// =====================================================
// === Packs                                         ===
// =====================================================
pack.localappdata.name: %LOCALAPPDATA%
pack.localappdata.description: Application data directory (%LOCALAPPDATA%\.llmassist)
pack.useragentshome.name: User Agents Home
pack.useragentshome.description: User-scoped agents home
pack.agentshome.name: Workspace Agents Home
pack.agentshome.description: Workspace-scoped agents home
pack.workdir.name: Working Directory
pack.workdir.description: The working directory itself, treated as an addon pack.
pack.source.unknown: Unknown
pack.source.workingdirectory: Working Directory
pack.source.appdata: App Data
pack.source.useragentshome: User Agents
pack.source.agentshome: Workspace Agents
pack.source.configuration: Configuration
pack.source.scanned: Scanned

// =====================================================
// === Settings UI                                   ===
// =====================================================
settings.title: Addons
settings.search_folders: Search Folders
settings.search_folders.hint: These folders are searched for addon packs inside the user profile and each working directory.
settings.additional_search_folders: Additional Search Folders
settings.additional_search_folders.hint: Global setting, applies to ALL chats (all chat profiles): these folders are searched for addon packs inside the user profile and each working directory, in addition to the default ones.
settings.search_folder.placeholder: Folder name (e.g. .agents)...
settings.workdirs: Working Directories
settings.workdirs.hint: Configure how working directories participate in addon loading.
settings.fetch_all: Fetch addons from all working directories
settings.fetch_all.hint: When enabled, addon packs from all enabled working directories are loaded. Otherwise, only the current working directory is used.
settings.use_workdirs_as_packs: Use working directories as packs
settings.use_workdirs_as_packs.hint: When enabled, each working directory itself is treated as an addon pack.
settings.additional_pack_paths: Additional Pack Paths
settings.additional_pack_paths.hint: Direct paths to addon packs, similar to '~/.agents/packs/my-pack/'.
settings.additional_pack_paths.placeholder: Path to an addon pack...
settings.select_pack_folder: Select addon pack folder
settings.select_directory: Choose directory...
settings.select_file: Choose file...
settings.addon_sources: Additional Sources per Type
settings.addon_sources.hint: Add extra directories and files for each registered addon type (e.g. skills, tools, sub-agents).
settings.addon_sources.empty: No addon types registered yet
settings.addon_sources.directories: Directories
settings.addon_sources.directories.hint: Additional folders that will be scanned for addons of this type.
settings.addon_sources.files: Files
settings.addon_sources.files.hint: Individual files that will be loaded as addons of this type.
settings.packs: Addon Packs
settings.packs.hint: Enable or disable configurable addon packs. Non-configurable (implicit) packs are always enabled and shown for reference.
settings.packs.empty: No addon packs found
settings.packs.refresh: Refresh
settings.packs.search.placeholder: Search addon packs...
settings.packs.filter.all: All
settings.packs.filter.configurable: Configurable
settings.enable_packs_by_default: Enable packs by default
settings.enable_packs_by_default.hint: When checked, packs without an explicit override are enabled by default. Uncheck to disable all unchanged packs.
settings.pack.enabled: Enabled
settings.pack.disabled: Disabled
settings.pack.manifest_invalid: Invalid manifest
settings.pack.source: Source
settings.directory.placeholder: Path...
settings.file.placeholder: File path...

// =====================================================
// === Addon types                                   ===
// =====================================================
type.skills.name: Skills
type.skills.description: Reusable skill procedures (SKILL.md files) that teach agents how to perform specific tasks.
type.templates.name: Prompt Templates
type.templates.description: Reusable prompt templates (LLT files) that define prompt parts for chats and agents: system prompts, personas, specializations, components, skills and sub-agents.
type.tools.name: Tools
type.tools.description: Scriptable tool definitions (Lua, Python and C# scripts) that are exposed to the LLM as callable tools.
type.scripts.lua.name: Lua-scripts
type.scripts.lua.description: Scripts written in Lua, used for Lua-based tools and used for hooks registration.
type.agents.name: Sub-agents
type.agents.description: Reusable sub-agents (agent.md files) that define specialist personas with their own tools, skills, sub-agents and memory blocks.
type.context.name: Prompt contexts
type.context.description: The sections the system prompt of an agent is assembled from (identity, skills, sub-agents, memory blocks, tools, working directories and others).
type.commands.name: Slash commands
type.commands.description: User-triggered commands (/skill:<name>, /agent:<name>) that inject a skill's body or launch a sub-agent from the start of a message.

// =====================================================
// === Diagnostics                                   ===
// =====================================================
diagnostic.fileaccesserror: File Access Error
diagnostic.fileaccesserror.hint: Unable to read the addon file. Check file permissions.
diagnostic.generalparsingerror: Parse Error
diagnostic.generalparsingerror.hint: An unexpected error occurred while parsing the addon file.
diagnostic.missingdescription: Missing Description
diagnostic.missingdescription.hint: The addon has no description. Add a description in YAML frontmatter or as the first paragraph.
diagnostic.missingfile: File Missing
diagnostic.missingfile.hint: The addon file could not be found at the expected location.
diagnostic.missingname: Missing Name
diagnostic.missingname.hint: The addon has no name defined in YAML frontmatter, header, or folder name.
diagnostic.missingyaml: Missing YAML
diagnostic.missingyaml.hint: The addon file does not have a YAML frontmatter block (--- ... ---).
diagnostic.missingyamldescription: Missing YAML Description
diagnostic.missingyamldescription.hint: The 'description' field is missing from the YAML frontmatter. A fallback was used.
diagnostic.missingyamlname: Missing YAML Name
diagnostic.missingyamlname.hint: The 'name' field is missing from the YAML frontmatter. A fallback name was used.
diagnostic.namedirectorymismatch: Name/Directory Mismatch
diagnostic.namedirectorymismatch.hint: The addon name does not match the name of the directory containing the addon file.
diagnostic.nameformaterror: Invalid Name Format
diagnostic.nameformaterror.hint: The addon name contains invalid characters. Addon names must use lowercase letters, digits and hyphens.
diagnostic.yamldecodingerror: YAML Decode Error
diagnostic.yamldecodingerror.hint: Failed to deserialize the YAML frontmatter into the expected structure.
diagnostic.yamlparsingerror: YAML Syntax Error
diagnostic.yamlparsingerror.hint: The YAML frontmatter contains invalid syntax.
